'''Vajdila''' ([[Qymish language|Qymish]]: Ⰲⰰⱜⰴⰹⰾⰰ) is a [[Qym]]ish [[wikipedia:crown corporation|crown corporation]] that designs and manufactures airplanes, rotorcraft, rockets, satellites, and missiles. 

==History==

==Budget and management==
Vajdila is operated as an independent crown corporation and receives a subsidy from the [[Royal Ministry of Defense (Qym)|Royal Ministry of Defense]] for research and development. Unlike the domestic-oriented [[Ramiq]], Vajdila's mission is both domestic and for export markets. As such, most Vajdila products are also exported outside of Qym. 

==Products==
===Passenger aircraft===
*[[Vajdila H-50]] (Narrow-body turboprop with 50 PAX; similar to the [[wikipedia:ATR 42|ATR 42]])
*[[Vajdila H-60]] (Narrow-body jet with 50-100 PAX; similar to the [[wikipedia:Embraer E-Jet E2 family|Embraer E175]])
*[[Vajdila H-70]] (Narrow-body jet with 100-150 PAX; similar to the [[wikipedia:Embraer E-Jet E2 family|Embraer E190]]/[[wikipedia:Embraer E-Jet E2 family|E195]])
*[[Vajdila H-80]] (Narrow-body jet with 150-200 PAX; similar to the [[wikipedia:Airbus A320 family|Airbus A320]])
*[[Vajdila H-90]] (Narrow-body jet with 200-250 PAX; similar to the [[wikipedia:Airbus A320 family|Airbus A321]])
*[[Vajdila H-850]] (Wide-body jet with 250-300 PAX; similar to the [[wikipedia:Boeing_777#777-200ER|Boeing 777-200ER]])
*[[Vajdila H-855]] (Wide-body jet with 200-250 PAX and extended range; similar to the [[wikipedia:Boeing_787_Dreamliner#787-8|Boeing 787-8]])
*[[Vajdila H-875]] (Wide-body jet with 300-350 PAX; similar to the [[wikipedia:Boeing_777#777-300ER_(B77W)|Boeing 777-300ER]])

===Military aircraft===
*[[Vajdila V-17]] (4th-generation multirole fighter; similar to the [[wikipedia:Sukhoi Su-27|Su-27]], [[wikipedia:Shenyang J-16|J-16]] and [[wikipedia:McDonnell Douglas F/A-18 Hornet|F-18]])
*[[Vajdila V-33]] (5th-generation stealth multirole fighter; similar to the [[wikipedia:Sukhoi Su-57|Su-57]], [[wikipedia:Lockheed Martin F-35 Lightning II|F-35]] and [[wikipedia:Shenyang J-35|J-35]])
*[[Vajdila H-81]] (Military variant of the Vajdila H-80)
**[[Vajdila H-81A]] (AEW&C)
**[[Vajdila H-81B]] 
**[[Vajdila H-81C]]
**[[Vajdila H-81D]] (SIGINT)
**[[Vajdila H-81E]] (Electronic warfare)
**[[Vajdila H-81F]]
**[[Vajdila H-81G]] (Maritime patrol)
*[[Vajdila H-900]] (Wide-body turboprop; similar to the [[wikipedia:Airbus A400M Atlas|Airbus A400M Atlas]])

